# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ASan build (docs/sanitizers.md).
#
# Third-party one-time allocations only. A leak whose allocation stack goes through our own
# code to our own allocation is a bug to fix, not to list here. Each entry says why it is not
# ours and why it is bounded.

# Exiv2 keeps custom XMP namespaces (metadata-util registers FLIR once per process) in a static
# registry whose destructor does not free the copied strings; only
# XmpProperties::unregisterNs() does. 2 allocations, once per helper process. The leak is in the
# metadata-util helper program, not in libddb: the helper is built with the same sanitizers and
# inherits LSAN_OPTIONS (this file) from the test that starts it. A leak found in a helper does
# not fail the test that ran it: the helper exits non-zero (LeakSanitizer's 23) when the pool
# closes it, and libddb logs that as a WARNING with the exit status and the end of the helper's
# stderr.
leak:Exiv2::XmpProperties::registerNs

# corto (vendor/libnexus/vendor/nexus/src/corto, upstream cnr-isti-vclab/corto): when a nexus
# node has fewer than 4 vertices, Encoder::encodeMesh() calls BitStream::reserve(nvert/4 == 0),
# which allocates new uint32_t[0] but records allocated = 0, so ~BitStream never frees it.
# One empty allocation per such node.
leak:crt::BitStream::reserve
